course: dictionary
lesson: 14513
title: Words for food: pepperoni
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pepperoni is a noun, a naming word for something you can eat. You can count some nouns, like one apple or two apples, but pepperoni is not counted like that. You say «Can I have some pepperoni?» or «a slice of pepperoni».
explain: Context helps you see what kind of food it is. «I'd like a pepperoni pizza, please!» Pizza is a food, so pepperoni is something that goes on top of or with pizza. «She ate three slices of pepperoni.» Slices tells you it is cut thin.
explain: Pepperoni is a spicy dried sausage, usually made of pork and beef. In maths, pizza slices are a good way to learn fractions. If a pizza has 8 equal slices and 2 of them have pepperoni, then 2 out of 8 slices have pepperoni.
fact: Pepperoni is a spicy dried sausage, usually made of pork and beef.
fact: Pepperoni is sliced thin and is often put on pizza.
fact: Pepperoni is uncountable, so we say «some pepperoni» or «a slice of pepperoni», not «two pepperonis».
fact: Pepperoni is a processed meat, which means it has been changed from fresh meat, for example by drying or curing.
fact: In maths, 2 slices out of 8 can be written as the fraction 2/8, which is the same as 1/4.
exercise: «I'd like a pepperoni pizza, please!» What is pepperoni? | A kind of bread roll | *A spicy dried sausage, often put on pizza | A cold drink with bubbles | A sweet fruit that grows on trees
exercise: «A pizza has 8 equal slices, and 2 slices have pepperoni.» What fraction of the pizza has pepperoni? | *2/8, which is the same as 1/4 | 3/8 | 8/2 | 1/8
exercise: «Pepperoni is a processed meat.» What does processed mean here? | *Changed from fresh meat, for example by drying or curing | Grown on a farm | Made only of vegetables | Sliced into thin pieces
test: Pepperoni is an uncountable noun. Which sentence is correct? | *I ate two slices of pepperoni | I ate two pepperoni | I ate pepperonis | I ate two pepperonis
test: Which sentence best describes pepperoni? | Cold and frozen like ice | Crunchy and green like a lettuce | Sweet and sticky like jam | *Spicy and dried, like a sausage
exam: Sam's pizza has 6 equal slices, and 3 of them have pepperoni. What fraction of the pizza has pepperoni? | *3/6, which is the same as 1/2 | 1/3 | 6/3 | 3/9
